    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d551">

                <pb facs="0725" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/159a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 22, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6103. For Gunther from War Trade Board:</p>
                <p>Reply to your cable 16th<anchor n="1" xml:id="d551-f1"/> delayed awaiting arrival
                    of McCormick, Taylor. Total Swedish tonnage is 1,300,000 dead-weight of which
                    they need for trade Sweden to Great Britain and America about 250,000 tons. We
                    must insist on balance being divided 50–50 with British. French should clearly
                    understand that this does not mean that the 50 per cent which we control will
                    not be partly allocated to them where their needs prove more urgent than any of
                    the other Allies. Of the quantity to be chartered to the Shipping Board
                    one-third to be in safe trades and two-thirds in transatlantic trade. Rates in
                    transatlantic to be same as inter-Allied chartering rates under Norwegian
                    agreement and in West Indian and South American trades to be that of American
                    Chartering Committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
